// What a braced body holds, which depends on the declaration.
//
// `define Name() { … }` holds one UI item and nothing else -- it is a named
// fragment of layout, and its body is the same grammar a `ui { }` block has.
// Everything else holds members: components, nested declarations, scripts.
//
// Parsing a define's body as members is what produced four diagnostics per
// component in flappy: `Col()[100, 100, top-center]` read as a component called
// `Col` followed by a bracket nothing expected, so every panel in the game
// reported its layout as a syntax error while the game itself still ran.

par_dbraced(int[] pos, int kd, int[] kids) {
  if (kd = (import ast_k_define)) {
    int item = par_item(pos);
    push(kids, item);
  } else {
    par_dinner(pos, kids);
  }
} return void;
